From ce3b84c7464008cff0299246c06b4e01b686934d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 01:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shore AR ladder batch: PE/BSS arm alignment and a targeted
 ZINB prototype

Harness 233 -> 264 assertions, 0 failing. Two code changes, both applied and
both testable, plus the batch that tests them:
06_diagnostics/run_shore_ar_zi_2026-09-03.R (~23-26 h, ships DRY_RUN = TRUE).

1. PE / BSS INCOMPLETE-TRIP ARM ALIGNMENT (Tier 2, closed).
The BSS learns R_G_boat from a frame that HAS been incomplete-trip filtered
(intA descends from int_d, after filter_incomplete_trips); both Point
Estimators built the same ratio from the UNFILTERED set.
sensitivity_incomplete_trips.csv has reported that as production_arm_bss
"exclude" vs production_arm_pe "gear_only" since 2026-08-25.

New shared helper 03_R_functions/pe_gear_ratio_frame.R, called by both PEs.
pe_gear_ratio_arm = "match_bss" ships; "gear_only" is retained for the
four-arm diagnostic and historical reproduction. MEASURED in stage P1 (PE
only, seconds): the boat PE moves 11,176 -> 11,170, -0.059%, and the shore
is unchanged, which is the control. A consistency fix, not an accuracy one.
One helper rather than two edits because the gear PE's comment already
claimed it matched the BSS while it did not.

2. ZERO-INFLATED CATCH LIKELIHOOD (Tier 3, prototype, ships OFF).
crab_bss_pooled.stan gains zi_catch, a Beta(1,9) prior and
vector<lower=0,upper=1>[zi_catch] theta_C, the zero-size guard pattern
shared_tau and f_lower use. Targeted from the 2026-09-01 zero bin: shore
all-gear 676 observed zeros vs 605.4 expected (z = +3.8, n = 1,649), shore
pot closure z = +2.9, every boat stream inside |z| = 2.3.

  * generated-quantities log_lik MIRRORS the fitted mixture. A log_lik under
    a different likelihood from the one fitted voids every elpd_loo
    comparison, and elpd is the entire basis for judging this.
  * THE SEASON TOTAL IS SCALED BY (1 - theta_C). lambda_C is fitted to the
    non-inflated component and rises to absorb the zeros theta_C removed, so
    an unscaled total would be inflated by 1/(1 - theta_C) purely by turning
    the feature on.
  * zi_catch is set PER FIT from catch_zi_populations (default "shore"), so
    one run carries the shore fits as treatment and the boat fits as an
    untouched negative control at no extra cost.
  Model compiles to C++ in 3.1 min.

THE BATCH
  P1  PE arm alignment ............  seconds, PE only, runs in the dry run
  G1  gear track with the driver fix  ~35 min, restores the cross-check
  Z0  ZINB present, OFF ...........  GATE and the ladder's DAILY rung
  A1  shore all-gear AR weekly ....  }  the main question: 29% of the port
  A2  shore all-gear AR biweekly ..  }  total, four rungs, one thing moving
  A3  shore all-gear AR monthly ...  }
  Z1  ZINB ON, shore only .........  boat fits are a free negative control

Z0 does two jobs deliberately: without its second, the ladder would compare
three post-edit rungs against a pre-edit production run. The ladder is read
in the order that settled the boat 2x2: randomized-PIT coverage, then p_loo
as a fraction of n_obs with the Pareto k count, then the CATCH stream's
elpd. Production sits at daily with p_loo 35.2%, 41 Pareto k > 0.7 and
coverage 0.701 (+7.1 SD); the gear track's monthly gives 0.035 (-16.4 SD).
Both ends are bad and the middle has never been run.

Verified: harness 264/264; new batch dry run (pre-flight 96 Stan data vars
all built, P1 PASS); stage5 self-test 22/22; validation batch 11 desk
criteria; all three Stan models pass stanc and the pooled one compiles to
C++; both drivers purl and parse; 37 helpers parse.

