+| `test_improvements_2026-08-25.R` | Dependency-light regression harness (no rstan, seconds to run) for the functions the 2026-08-25 batch added or changed, plus a guard on the shipped defaults in `run_config.R`, on the sampler-override whitelist, on the retro audit tables, and on the Stage 5 runner's hard-coded baselines. **264 assertions.** Run it before committing to any long fit. |
 | `run_stage5_2026-08-30.R` | Unattended batch for Stage 5 of `improvement-plan-2026-08-27.md`: S1 PE-fill re-run (minutes, no MCMC), S2 the `shared_tau` informed-day floor as an exact per-population bit-identity GATE, S3 the gear-track cross-check with the pooled track's sampler settings, S4a/S4b the tau x AR 2x2 (two runs, not one; stage F is not a matched control), S5 the uncontaminated boat pot-closure AR re-run. Ships with `DRY_RUN <- TRUE`, which resolves every config, runs the R-to-Stan data-contract pre-flight and a 22-assertion extractor self-test against the archived runs, and fits nothing. Roughly 18-24 h with `DRY_RUN <- FALSE`; resumable. **Ran 2026-08-30** (24 h; 11 of 12 criteria passing, the one FAIL being a criterion compared against a reference that differed in two ways); results reviewed in `07_documentation/development_notes/stage5-batch-review-2026-08-31.md`. |
 | `run_validation_2026-09-01.R` | The outstanding validation and diagnosis work after the 2026-09-01 adoption. FOUR DESK STAGES (D1-D4) that run during the dry run, need no Stan toolchain, and score backlog items against data already on disk: the Tier-1 shore I/E unit fix against its four pre-set criteria, the `gear_only` arm decision and the PE-vs-BSS arm disagreement, the PPC coverage and zero-bin reads, and a repository-hygiene audit. Then FIVE FITTED STAGES: V1 the adoption gate (production as shipped must reproduce S2 exactly), V2/V3 the never-sampled GR-7 Phase 2 Dirichlet gear shares with its control, V4 the untested shared-turnover x biweekly-pot-closure corner, V5 a `shared_tau_min_obs = 20` sensitivity. Ships `DRY_RUN <- TRUE`; roughly 15-17 h with it FALSE; resumable. **Ran 2026-09-01** (14.1 h; 17 of 19 criteria resolving, one FAIL a real production defect and one a criterion using the wrong reference); reviewed in `07_documentation/development_notes/validation-batch-review-2026-09-02.md`. |
